.TH UBUCARGO 1 "2026-10-20" "ubucargo" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ubucargo \- create and maintain Ubuntu packages for Rust crates
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ubucargo package
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ INPUT " [" VERSION ]]
.br
.B ubucargo deps
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ INPUT " [" VERSION ]]
.br
.B ubucargo
.RB { \-h | \-\-help | \-V | \-\-version }
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ubucargo
wraps debcargo to create and maintain Ubuntu source packages for Rust crates.
It keeps configuration and generated-file ownership state inside the package's
.B debian
directory, alongside maintainer changes.
Package generation requires debcargo 2.8.2 or a later compatible 2.x release.
.PP
Ubucargo is experimental; its command-line interface may change.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS package
Create or update a Debian source tree and orig tarball.
The source tree includes upstream sources, Debian packaging, and configuration.
The orig tarball is placed beside the source directory.
Regeneration uses
.B debian/debcargo.toml
and preserves maintainer overrides.
Generated alternatives to overridden files are written to corresponding
.B .debcargo.hint
files.
Ambiguous ownership may require an explicit
.B \-\-keep
or
.B \-\-replace
decision.
.PP
When upgrading to a new upstream release or repacking the source, ubucargo
compares the working tree with the old and new upstream sources.
Files unchanged from the old upstream are updated automatically, and local
additions are retained when compatible with the new upstream.
Source conflicts require maintainer resolution or
.BR \-\-force .
Updates are staged and validated before writing to the destination.
Full generation restores applied quilt patches to their original position in staging.
Use
.B \-\-prepare-only
to prepare the source and automatic patches for maintainer patch porting,
leaving all patches unapplied.
.PP
Regenerating a released package creates a new
.B UNRELEASED
changelog entry; subsequent runs update that entry.
.SS deps
Inspect archive candidates for the direct Rust library dependencies needed to
build and install the selected package's binary packages and run applicable
autopkgtests.
For local and published source packages, this inspection is based on the existing control files;
for crates.io and local Cargo inputs, it is based on temporary packaging generated with default
configuration.
This command leaves existing package files unchanged.
.PP
Each dependency is checked independently for compatible package names,
Debian version constraints, and features.
The report groups dependencies by binary package, source, and test, and
classifies candidates as
.BR selected ,
.BR available ,
.BR incompatible ,
.BR missing ,
or
.BR unknown .
Complex dependency alternatives are reported as
.B unknown
for manual assessment.
Use
.BR sbuild (1)
and
.BR autopkgtest (1)
to validate complete build and test environments, including transitive
dependencies and joint installability.
.SS help
Print general help or help for a subcommand with
.B ubucargo help
.RI [ COMMAND ].
.SH INPUT AND VERSION SELECTION
Both commands accept the following input selectors.
Paths are relative to the working directory.
.TP
.BI crate: NAME
Select a crates.io crate.
A bare
.I NAME
has the same meaning.
.I VERSION
selects an exact Cargo version; the default is the latest eligible stable,
non-yanked release.
An exact request may select a prerelease or yanked release.
Crates published only as prereleases require an exact version.
.TP
.BI ubuntu: SUITE / SOURCE
Select a published Ubuntu source package by its Debian source name.
.IB SUITE / SOURCE
is shorthand for the same input.
A base series selects release, updates, and security in main and universe.
A suite ending in
.BR \-updates ,
.BR \-security ,
.BR \-proposed ,
or
.B \-backports
selects that pocket alone.
.I VERSION
selects an exact Debian source version; the default is the highest published
version in the selected indexes.
.TP
.BI debian: SUITE / SOURCE
Select a published Debian source package from the exact named suite in main.
.I VERSION
selects an exact Debian source version; the default is the highest published
version in that suite.
.TP
.BI ppa: OWNER / NAME / SERIES / SOURCE
Select a published source package from a public Launchpad PPA.
All four fields are required.
.I VERSION
selects an exact Debian source version; the default is the highest published
version in the selected Ubuntu series.
.TP
.BI pkg: PATH
Select an existing source package containing
.BR debian/changelog .
An input of
.BR . ,
.BR .. ,
or a path beginning with
.BR ./ ,
.BR ../ ,
or
.B /
also selects a source package.
The package supplies its current version.
.TP
.BI local: PATH
Select a local Cargo crate containing a root
.BR Cargo.toml ,
which supplies the version.
For
.BR package ,
.B \-\-package-dir
is required, and the input and destination must be separate, non-nested
directory trees.
.PP
Omitting
.I INPUT
selects the nearest directory at or above the working directory containing
.BR debian/changelog .
.SH PACKAGE OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-package-dir " DIR"
Select the destination directory.
Package inputs default to their existing directory; a different destination
receives a regenerated copy and must be new.
Published inputs require a new destination, defaulting to
.BI ./ SOURCE .
Crates.io inputs default to the nearest parent source package, or to the
unsuffixed Debian source name in the working directory.
For crates.io and local Cargo inputs, an existing destination supplies
configuration and maintainer changes for the same crate.
.TP
.BI \-\-config " PATH"
Use the supplied debcargo configuration to create a new package from crates.io
or a local Cargo input, and save it as
.BR debian/debcargo.toml .
The configuration path is relative to the working directory.
Relative local source paths are resolved against the supplied configuration's
directory and rebased for the destination.
An explicit
.B local:
input supplies the local source path in preference to the configured value.
Existing packages and published source inputs use their own
.BR debian/debcargo.toml .
.TP
.B \-\-prepare-only
Prepare upstream source, the orig tarball, changelog, and fresh automatic patches
for maintainer patch porting, without regenerating packaging.
A fresh crate input receives minimal packaging: configuration, changelog,
source format, and any automatic patches and their series.
Existing inputs retain their maintained packaging, hints, and ownership manifest;
automatic patches and their series entries are replaced with the fresh set.
.TP
.B \-\-force
Resolve source-tree conflicts by adopting the selected upstream state for
paths owned by either the old or new upstream tree.
Local-only paths remain preserved.
The old orig tarball is required as the merge baseline, and an existing
destination orig tarball must match the generated contents.
.TP
.BI \-\-keep " PATH"
Preserve an ambiguous primary file when ownership baselines are missing or
conflict, and record the fresh generated state.
Write a hint when a generated alternative exists and differs.
.I PATH
is relative to the package directory.
Repeat this option for multiple paths.
.TP
.BI \-\-replace " PATH"
Adopt a managed path's freshly generated contents and permissions, or delete
the primary if generation produces absence.
Remove its hint and record fresh generated state for paths supporting
maintainer overrides.
.I PATH
is relative to the package directory.
Repeat this option for multiple paths.
Each path may be named by only one of
.B \-\-keep
and
.BR \-\-replace .
.SH DEPS OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-suite " SUITE"
Select the dependency-checking environment as
.BI ubuntu: SUITE
or
.BI debian: SUITE .
A bare suite name selects Ubuntu.
Debian inputs default to their exact suite; Ubuntu and PPA inputs default to
their base Ubuntu series.
Crates.io and local inputs default to the current Ubuntu development series
reported by
.BR "ubuntu-distro-info \-\-devel" .
A base Ubuntu series selects release, updates, and security in main and
universe; a suite with a pocket suffix selects that pocket alone.
A Debian suite selects exactly that suite in main.
.TP
.B \-\-proposed
Include the proposed pocket of a base Ubuntu checking suite.
Requires an Ubuntu checking suite.
.TP
.BI \-\-ppa " ppa:OWNER/NAME"
Add a public Launchpad PPA for the checking suite's base Ubuntu series.
Repeat this option for multiple PPAs.
Requires an Ubuntu checking suite.
For Ubuntu checking suites, a PPA input also automatically includes its PPA.
.TP
.BI \-\-architecture " ARCH"
Select the Debian architecture used to check dependencies and filter
autopkgtests.
Defaults to the host's native architecture as reported by
.BR "dpkg \-\-print-architecture" .
.SH COMMON OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-keep-staging
Retain and print temporary staging directories for inspection, including
on failure.
Available with both subcommands.
.TP
.BI \-\-crates-io-api " URL"
Use
.I URL
as the crates.io metadata API base URL.
Defaults to
.BR https://crates.io/api/v1 .
Available with both subcommands.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help for the command or subcommand.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the program version.
Available on the top-level command.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disable colored dependency output when set.
Redirected output is plain text.
.TP
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
Store the shared APT metadata cache under
.BR $XDG_CACHE_HOME/ubucargo/apt .
.TP
.B HOME
When
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
is unset, store the APT cache under
.BR $HOME/.cache/ubucargo/apt .
.TP
.BR DEBFULLNAME ", " DEBEMAIL
Name and email address used for changelog entries, which are written with
.BR dch (1).
.SH FILES
.TP
.B debian/debcargo.toml
Package generation configuration.
A relative
.B crate_src_path
is resolved against the directory containing this file.
.TP
.B debian/ubucargo-state.json
Latest generated content hashes and executable status used to recognize
maintainer overrides during regeneration.
.TP
.IB PATH .debcargo.hint
Latest generated alternative for an overridden packaging file.
Adopting the hint's contents and permissions allows automatic updates to
resume on the next run.
.TP
.B ~/.cache/ubucargo/apt/
Shared, signature-verified APT metadata cache, used for dependency inspection
and published source selection.
Each invocation refreshes the selected indexes and reuses unchanged data.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Successful package generation or preparation, or every reported direct Rust dependency has
a compatible candidate.
Help and version requests also exit successfully.
.TP
.B 1
Dependency inspection completed with at least one incompatible, missing,
or unknown dependency.
.TP
.B 2
Command-line, generation, source-conflict, network, metadata, or other error.
.SH EXAMPLES
Create or update the latest serde package:
.PP
.nf
.RS
ubucargo package serde
.RE
.fi
.PP
Select an exact release and destination:
.PP
.nf
.RS
ubucargo package serde 1.0.220 \-\-package-dir ./rust-serde
.RE
.fi
.PP
Regenerate the source package containing the working directory:
.PP
.nf
.RS
ubucargo package
.RE
.fi
.PP
Create a package from a local Cargo crate:
.PP
.nf
.RS
ubucargo package local:../example \-\-package-dir ./rust-example
.RE
.fi
.PP
Prepare another upstream release for patch porting, then generate packaging:
.PP
.nf
.RS
ubucargo package serde 1.0.229 \-\-package-dir ./rust-serde \-\-prepare-only
cd rust-serde
# Port the maintained patches with quilt.
ubucargo package
.RE
.fi
.PP
Preserve a maintainer's control file when ownership is ambiguous:
.PP
.nf
.RS
ubucargo package \-\-keep debian/control
.RE
.fi
.PP
Inspect a crates.io crate against Debian unstable:
.PP
.nf
.RS
ubucargo deps serde \-\-suite debian:unstable
.RE
.fi
.PP
Inspect Ubuntu packaging against another Ubuntu series with a PPA:
.PP
.nf
.RS
ubucargo deps ubuntu:resolute/rust-serde \-\-suite jammy \e
    \-\-ppa ppa:owner/staging
.RE
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR debcargo (1),
.BR cargo (1),
.BR dch (1),
.BR quilt (1),
.BR sbuild (1),
.BR autopkgtest (1)
.PP
Detailed command specifications and cache documentation are available in
the project's
.BR docs/
directory:
.UR https://github.com/canonical/ubucargo
.UE
